              <description>Include swing calibration during startup</description>
              <lsb>5</lsb>
              <msb>5</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>INITIAL_START_ENABLE</name>
              <description>Whether to enable 'initial start' or not (whenever retriggering startup). 'initial start' re-initializes EstKdtc</description>
              <lsb>6</lsb>
              <msb>6</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>COLD_START_ENABLE</name>
              <description>Whether to enable 'cold start' or not (whenever retriggering startup). 'cold start' initializes even more. During a cold start, phaseSelect randomization is forced on</description>
              <lsb>7</lsb>
              <msb>7</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FSM_NO_INIT_RESET</name>
              <description>Backdoor which prevents r_initial_start from being set low when receiving a channel switch trigger while being in the TRK state</description>
              <lsb>8</lsb>
              <msb>8</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FSM_COLD_START_NO_INIT_RESET</name>
              <description>Backdoor which prevents r_cold_start from being set low when receiving a channel switch trigger while being in the TRK state</description>
              <lsb>9</lsb>
              <msb>9</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PHASE_DETECT_ENABLE</name>
              <description>Selects whether phase detect of the output from the counter should be enabled or not</description>
              <lsb>10</lsb>
              <msb>10</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DTC_DEM_EN</name>
              <description>Connected directly to the output signal 'dtcDemEn'</description>
              <lsb>11</lsb>
              <msb>11</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TDC_FORCE_ZERO</name>
              <description>Force the binary TDC output from tdcRealign to the TRK bank control to zero. This basically opens up the loop</description>
              <lsb>12</lsb>
              <msb>12</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FORCE_CORE_EXT_CLOCK_ON</name>
              <description>By default the clock to AdPllCoreExt is stopped when the state machine is not active. If setting this to 1, the clock is always on</description>
              <lsb>13</lsb>
              <msb>13</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BUFFER_MEM_UPDATE</name>
              <description>When 1, we will wait until the uni trigger arrives before applying changes to normPvtMem, normAcqMem and normTrkMem</description>
              <lsb>14</lsb>
              <msb>14</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RUN_TRK</name>
              <description>When 1, TRK will run normally. When 0 TRK will stay silent when entered to TRK state.</description>
              <lsb>15</lsb>
              <msb>15</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FSCOMMANDADDR</name>
              <description>Address for the async interface. ALWAYS 0x100.</description>
              <lsb>16</lsb>
              <msb>27</msb>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>VARIOUS_ENABLE1_ADDR</name>
                  <description>ALWAYS 0x100.</description>
                  <value>0x100</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>READ</name>
              <description>When 1, a read transaction is initiated. When the event COMPLETETRANS is set, read back this register</description>
              <lsb>31</lsb>
              <msb>31</msb>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>FSCOMMAND_VARIOUS_ENABLE2</name>
          <description>Send or receive command directly to/from the AdPllLte digital island. Only write to this register when FSASYNCBUSBUSY returns 0</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0400</addressOffset>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x02349A84</resetValue>
          <alternateRegister>FSCOMMAND_ANA_ISOLATION</alternateRegister>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>ESTIMATORS_ON_FOR_INT_CH</name>
              <description>When 0, estkdtc and estdutycycle is not active for integer channels</description>
              <lsb>1</lsb>
              <msb>1</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PAUSE_CLOCK_AT_DCO_ENABLE</name>
              <description>If 1, when DCO gets enabled we temporarily stop the clock since there is a glitch-risk</description>
              <lsb>2</lsb>
              <msb>2</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ALWAYS_SWING_TDC_OFFSET_CAL</name>
              <description>If 1, swing and TDC offet calibration is performed every time new frequency is triggered with full start</description>
              <lsb>3</lsb>
              <msb>3</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>EST_KDTC_ALWAYS_USE_ONLY_SIGN</name>
              <description>If 1, estkdtc only uses sign also outside packet</description>
              <lsb>5</lsb>
              <msb>5</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DISABLE_FASTER_GEARING</name>
              <description>For adding backwards compatibility: When requesting frequency reload together with back-to-TRK, the gearing happens twice as fast as during normal PLL startup if this register is not set. It also happens twice as fast when loading a phase change with the PHASE_CHANGE register</description>
              <lsb>6</lsb>
              <msb>6</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PVT_MOVING_AVERAGE_FILTER_EN</name>
              <description>Enable the moving average filter in the PVT bank control</description>
              <lsb>7</lsb>
              <msb>7</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PVT_MOVING_AVERAGE_FILTER_MODE</name>
              <description>When 1, the filtered value is used also during calibration</description>
              <lsb>8</lsb>
              <msb>8</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ACQ_MOVING_AVERAGE_FILTER_EN</name>
              <description>Enable the moving average filter in the ACQ bank control</description>
              <lsb>9</lsb>
              <msb>9</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ACQ_MOVING_AVERAGE_FILTER_MODE</name>
              <description>When 1, the filtered value is used also during calibration</description>
              <lsb>10</lsb>
              <msb>10</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FREEZE_KDTC_WHEN_RELOAD_FREQ</name>
              <description>When loading new frequency, we temporarily freeze the kDTC estimator. This is mostly interesting when staying in TRK bank state, because when going back to PVT or ACQ state, the kDTC estimator is anyway disabled for a while.</description>
              <lsb>11</lsb>
              <msb>11</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ACQ_OVERFLOW_RESET_KDTC</name>
              <description>When the ACQ bank overflows, we reset the KDTC estimator to the middle</description>
              <lsb>12</lsb>
              <msb>12</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>IGNORE_KDTC_ACCU_RECOVERY_VAL</name>
              <description>If set to 1, we do not use the recovery value of the kDTC accumulator captured during the first lock after power-up.</description>
              <lsb>13</lsb>
              <msb>13</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RELOCK_SOFT_SETS_COLD_INIT</name>
              <description>Always execute cold start init when using trigger uniTriggerRelockBackToAcq or uniTriggerRelockBackToTrk.</description>
              <lsb>14</lsb>
              <msb>14</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DTC_ON_PVT_ACQ</name>
              <description>When 1, the AdPllDtcCtrl runs already during PVT and ACQ calibration. When 0, the AdPllDtcCtrl only starts when in TRK</description>
              <lsb>15</lsb>
              <msb>15</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FSCOMMANDADDR</name>
              <description>Address for the async interface. ALWAYS 0x234.</description>
              <lsb>16</lsb>
              <msb>27</msb>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>VARIOUS_ENABLE2_ADDR</name>
                  <description>ALWAYS 0x234.</description>
                  <value>0x234</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>READ</name>
              <description>When 1, a read transaction is initiated. When the event COMPLETETRANS is set, read back this register</description>
              <lsb>31</lsb>
              <msb>31</msb>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>ENABLE</name>
          <description>Enable AdPllCompanionLte IP</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0404</addressOffset>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>ENABLE</name>
              <description>Enable the IP</description>
              <lsb>0</lsb>
              <msb>0</msb>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>Reset</name>
                  <description>IP core synchronous reset</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>Enable</name>
                  <description>Enable</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>CONFIG</name>
          <description>Common configurations of AdPllCompanionLte</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0408</addressOffset>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>REQUESTCLOCKOVERRIDE</name>
              <description>Force requesting clock</description>
              <lsb>0</lsb>
              <msb>0</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RELOADFREQWILLTRIGGER</name>
              <description>Set up the specific unitrigger to be activated when a frequency reload request is made through TASKS_RELOADFREQINTERNAL</description>
              <lsb>1</lsb>
              <msb>2</msb>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>changeFreq_restart</name>
                  <description>RF frequency will be switched, and the state machine will start from the first state</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>changeFreq_backToACQ</name>
                  <description>RF frequency will be switched and the state machine will go back to the ACQ2 state</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>changeFreq_backToFastTRK</name>
                  <description>RF frequency will be switched and the TRK bank will switch temporarily to the fastest gear</description>
                  <value>0x2</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>changeFreq_TRK</name>
                  <description>RF frequency will be reloaded while the loop is operating as normal</description>
                  <value>0x3</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>FSCLOCKSELECT</name>
          <description>Back-up solution: Set the clock source for the AdPllLte digital island</description>
          <addressOffset>0x040C</addressOffset>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000001</resetValue>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>SRC</name>
              <description>Select which clock source to be used in the AdPllLte digital island. Effective only when automatic clock switching is disabled in the AdPllLte digital island. 2'b00: ck64MCore, 2'b01: ckRetimed, 2'b10: ckRef</description>
              <lsb>0</lsb>
              <msb>1</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>STOP</name>
              <description>Force-stopping the clock internally in the AdPllLte island</description>
              <lsb>2</lsb>
              <msb>2</msb>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>START</name>
              <description>Start the clock again after the AdPllLte island stops the clock by its own</description>
              <lsb>3</lsb>
              <msb>3</msb>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
